Q: initialising multiple empty lists A: <p>IEnumerable is the most basic interface for collections. <br>Using this, you can instantiate any type of collection dynamically.</p>
<p>For empty lists, use.
<pre><code>Enumerable.Empty&lt;TYPE&gt;();
</code></pre>
<p>In your example...</p>
<pre><code>using System.Collections.Generic;
...
IEnumerable&lt;string&gt; Columns = Enumerable.Empty&lt;string&gt;();
IEnumerable&lt;string&gt; Parameters = Enumerable.Empty&lt;string&gt;();
IEnumerable&lt;string&gt; Values = Enumerable.Empty&lt;string&gt;();
</code></pre>
